  "reason": "The strongest evidence from the search is that the RNA encoder is the most impactful design choice: switching from PCA to scvi_n200 in the multimodal/multiprofile/ViT-L/avgpool/weighted setting yielded a large jump from 0.635 to 0.706. The next logical question is whether another learned encoder (scgpt) can match or exceed scvi_n200 in this same setting. config_049 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt + imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) isolates exactly this comparison while holding all other hyperparameters identical to the current best (config_037). This is the best use of experiment 9 because: (1) it directly tests the most important remaining uncertainty—whether a different learned RNA representation can further improve accuracy; (2) it changes only one variable relative to the best config, giving a clean comparison; and (3) with only one experiment remaining after this, testing the highest-leverage design axis (RNA encoder) in the proven best architecture maximizes the chance of finding a configuration that surpasses 0.706."
